invariant: INV-14
file: srv_auth.c
catches: srv_auth_test
reason: the ECDSA slot passes its public key to p256_ecdsa_verify without
  testing pub_len, and that verifier reads 64 bytes whatever the slot
  claims, so a shorter object is read past its end. srv_cfg.h states the
  64, and this length test is the only line that holds a caller to it.
  test/srv_auth_test.c sets pub_len one byte short and requires
  CH_EINVAL.

--- old
        return id->priv_len == P256_PRIV_LEN && id->pub_len == SRV_P256_PUB_LEN;
--- new
        return id->priv_len == P256_PRIV_LEN;
